  "debrief": "Logic chips are powered through their own pins: VCC (14) and GND (7) on nearly every 14-pin chip. Forget them and nothing works. The 10 kΩ pull-downs matter too: they hold each input low while its switch is off, because a CMOS input left floating reads high, low or anything in between."
